## Model card (unresolved — scaffolded placeholder)

- **Name:** Qwen 3.7 (as scaffolded)
- **Short description:** The dataset entry `qwen-3.7` (`opencode/qwen-3.7`) carries a **scaffolded** meta (`"scaffolded": true`; generic short "Qwen 3.7 model evaluation entry"; "Standard pricing"; "128K total"; "Text in/out"). Research indicates **"Qwen3.7" is a SERIES name, not a distinct plain model** — the released Qwen3.7 family is **Qwen3.7-Max** (`qwen-3.7-max`, my report 79), **Qwen3.7-Plus** (`qwen-3.7-plus`, my report 50), and **Qwen3.7-Flash** (a vision-language reasoning model). No standalone "Qwen3.7" instruct/base API model with its own spec sheet or benchmark table was found.
- **Provider / access:** No distinct `opencode/qwen-3.7` endpoint is documented; Alibaba Cloud Model Studio's supported-models list (Oct 2026) shows `qwen3.7-plus` / `qwen3.8-max`, **not** a plain `qwen3.7`.
- **Release / knowledge:** "Qwen3.7: The Agent Frontier" was announced ~May 19–21, 2026 as the **series** (Max/Plus/Flash). No separate plain-Qwen3.7 release was located.
- **IDs:** `opencode/qwen-3.7` (scaffold).
- **Context window:** meta scaffold claims "128K total" — **unverified**, and it matches none of Max (1M), Plus, or Flash.
- **Modalities:** meta scaffold claims "Text in/out" — **unverified**.
- **Pricing:** meta scaffold claims "Standard pricing" — **no verified numbers found**.
- **Architecture:** not published for any distinct plain "Qwen3.7".

