> Provenance / conclusion: every raw-benchmark row resolves to "no verified public score found" for this exact ID. The distinguishing benchmarks belong to the separately-slugged variants (Max → report 79; Plus → report 50). Rather than inherit the scaffold's unverified "128K / Text / Standard pricing" or borrow a variant's numbers (which would misattribute them to a model that may not exist), this entry is self-excluded.
> Note on the open-weight angle: press chatter references a "Qwen3.7 27B" open-weight release and "Qwen3.7-Flash" on OpenRouter — but a 27B open model would carry its own slug (cf. `qwen-3.8-27b`), and Flash is multimodal (not the scaffold's "Text in/out"). Neither maps cleanly to this plain `qwen-3.7` scaffold, and no benchmarks were found for either under this ID.
